                  "multiple": false,
                  "typeClass": "primitive",
                  "value": "Olympic Games"
                }
              },
              {
                "keywordValue": {
                  "typeName": "keywordValue",
                  "multiple": false,
                  "typeClass": "primitive",
                  "value": "Olympic athletes"
                }
              },
              {
                "keywordValue": {
                  "typeName": "keywordValue",
                  "multiple": false,
                  "typeClass": "primitive",
                  "value": "Foreign-born Olympians"
                }
              },
              {
                "keywordValue": {
                  "typeName": "keywordValue",
                  "multiple": false,
                  "typeClass": "primitive",
                  "value": "Olympic migration"
                }
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "typeName": "notesText",
            "multiple": false,
            "typeClass": "primitive",
            "value": "The data file has been updated on 11-07-2017. The outdated data file is no longer available.\n\nIf an athlete’s country of birth is unknown, a question mark is used. If an athlete’s country of birth is the same as the country represented, the cell is left empty. Athletes born in overseas territories of the United Kingdom, France, or the Netherlands (which do not have their own recognised National Olympic Committees) were marked native. Following Czaika and De Haas (2014), athletes are (retroactively) marked foreign-born or native based on today’s territorial borders.\n\nThe depositor provided the data file in XLSX format. DANS added the CSV format of this file to ensure preservation."
          },
